mutable renames with follow-mutable-history flag

  $ testtool_drawdag -R repo <<'EOF'
  > MR1-MR2
  > # modify: MR1 "old_name" "content for mutable rename test\n"
  > # modify: MR2 "new_name" "content for mutable rename test\n"
  > # delete: MR2 "old_name"
  > EOF
  MR1=* (glob)
  MR2=* (glob)

  $ mononoke_admin mutable-renames -R repo add \
  >   --src-commit-id "$MR1" --src-path old_name \
  >   --dst-commit-id "$MR2" --dst-path new_name
  Creating entry for source file `old_name` to destination file `new_name`

without --follow-mutable-history, new_name appears as added
  $ scsc diff --repo repo --paths-only -i "$MR2" -p new_name
  A new_name

with --follow-mutable-history, new_name is recognized as renamed from old_name
  $ scsc diff --repo repo --paths-only --follow-mutable-history -i "$MR2" -p new_name
  R old_name -> new_name

